  "instance_name": "rock_smoking",
  "label": "Smoking rocks (marijuana)",
  "description": "The phrase 'skip rocks, don't smoke them' implies a misunderstanding or misinterpretation of the word 'rocks'. In real-world context, 'rocks' can refer to the physical stones used in the activity of skipping, but also to marijuana (often called 'pot' or 'weed'), which is commonly smoked. The meme humorously points out the absurdity of someone smoking marijuana instead of skipping stones, using the word 'rocks' as a pun. This requires background knowledge of drug culture and slang terminology.",
